chived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2025-06-16T12:57:04Z","updated_at":"2025-06-17T13:46:56Z","closed_at":"2025-06-17T13:40:10Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.4.1.stable.arch_linux\n\n### System information\n\nEndeavourOS - v4.4.1.stable.arch_linux\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using an external editor (in my case Neovim) and having two projects open, only globals / autoloads from the first project the editor finds are recognized, which is not necessarily the project in which the file is located. This is only fixed after closing the first project and instance of Godot.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Make sure you're using an external editor (preferably one that directly uses the LSP, as full Godot extensions may have workarounds for this)\n- Create a new script\n- Add any variable and initialize it\n- Via `Project > Project Settings > Globals > Autoload` point to the script, name it, then press add and make sure the \"Global Variable\" box is checked\n- Create a second script and access the variable\n- Repeat this process with a second project\n- Without closing the first project or Editor, try to access the second project's global variables. The LSP will only provide autocomplete data and visually accept the ones from the first project, throwing errors with correct variables and not throwing them with incorrect ones. The project itself works fine despite this.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNote that when testing this without the `.godot` folder the LSP couldn't activate properly. I did still follow the instructions and leave it out in these 2 MRPs, maybe you have some standardized way of replacing the folder or something, but if you need it just ask.\n\n[Globals.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20757242/Globals.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"KeebCat","id":70770307,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzcwMzA3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70770307?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeebCat","html_url":"https://github.com/KeebCat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeebCat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeebCat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeebCat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeebCat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeebCat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeebCat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeebCat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeebCat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeebCat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107592/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107592/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}